# Git

Source: `governance/policies/git.md`

- Run `git status` before changing files; never overwrite, discard or stash the human's uncommitted changes unasked.
- Work on a feature branch (`<type>/<task-id>-<slug>`), not on the default branch, unless the project allows it.
- Commit only when asked or when the workflow defines it. Small, focused commits; Conventional Commits style.
- Never commit secrets, runtime state or unrelated changes.
- Merging is a human decision for MEDIUM risk and above.
- Prefer `git revert` over rewriting shared history.

## Never automatically (explicit approval every time)
`git reset --hard` · `git clean -f/-fd/-fdx` · `git push --force` / `--force-with-lease` · `git branch -D` ·
`git checkout -- <path>` / `git restore` on modified files · `git stash drop` / `clear` ·
rebase of shared branches · `git filter-branch` / `filter-repo` · deleting tags or remote branches.
